ATTORNEY: I want to move now to the afternoon of May 7, 2016. You told me

206
00:15:04,937 --> 00:15:11,050
ATTORNEY: earlier you were working the counter that day. What time did your shift start?

207
00:15:11,050 --> 00:15:16,050
WITNESS D: I came in at noon. I was supposed to go until eight.

208
00:15:16,050 --> 00:15:19,970
ATTORNEY: And who else was working with you that afternoon?

209
00:15:19,970 --> 00:15:24,273
WITNESS D: Nobody else on the floor. The manager had been in the

210
00:15:24,273 --> 00:15:28,170
WITNESS D: morning, but she'd left by then. It was just me.

211
00:15:28,170 --> 00:15:34,230
ATTORNEY: You described the afternoon as slow. Can you give me a sense of how slow?

212
00:15:34,230 --> 00:15:39,356
WITNESS D: Saturday afternoons it picks up around five, people coming back from the river

213
00:15:39,356 --> 00:15:44,220
WITNESS D: or the lake. Before that it's maybe a customer every ten, fifteen minutes.

214
00:15:44,220 --> 00:15:49,210
ATTORNEY: Between, say, four o'clock and four-thirty, do you remember any particular customers?

215
00:15:49,210 --> 00:15:53,609
WITNESS D: Not really particular. A man bought ice and gas. There was a

216
00:15:53,609 --> 00:15:58,154
WITNESS D: lady who bought some things and went back outside. A couple of

217
00:15:58,154 --> 00:16:02,040
WITNESS D: kids came in for drinks. That's about all I remember.

218
00:16:02,040 --> 00:16:07,750
ATTORNEY: The lady who bought some things and went back outside, did you know her?

219
00:16:07,750 --> 00:16:11,320
WITNESS D: No. I didn't know her before that day.

220
00:16:11,320 --> 00:16:14,170
ATTORNEY: Do you remember what she bought?

221
00:16:14,170 --> 00:16:18,800
WITNESS D: Not exactly. A few groceries, I think. She had a bag.

222
00:16:18,800 --> 00:16:24,870
ATTORNEY: After she went back outside, did you see her again before you heard anything unusual?

223
00:16:24,870 --> 00:16:28,790
WITNESS D: No. Once somebody goes out the door I can't really

224
00:16:28,790 --> 00:16:32,710
WITNESS D: see them. Like I said, the windows are covered up.

225
00:16:32,710 --> 00:16:35,888
ATTORNEY: Okay. Let's talk about what you heard. At some

226
00:16:35,888 --> 00:16:39,480
ATTORNEY: point that afternoon did you hear something unusual?

227
00:16:39,480 --> 00:16:43,410
WITNESS D: Yes. I heard a very loud bang. Really loud.

228
00:16:43,410 --> 00:16:46,970
ATTORNEY: Do you know about what time that was?

229
00:16:46,970 --> 00:16:51,223
WITNESS D: It was four-thirty-something. I remember because I'd just looked at

230
00:16:51,223 --> 00:16:54,460
WITNESS D: the clock over the cooler, thinking about my break.

231
00:16:54,460 --> 00:16:57,670
ATTORNEY: Can you describe the sound for me?

232
00:16:57,670 --> 00:17:01,164
WITNESS D: It was like a big crunch and a bang at the

233
00:17:01,164 --> 00:17:06,073
WITNESS D: same time. Metal. It was louder than anything I'd heard out

234
00:17:06,073 --> 00:17:10,150
WITNESS D: there, and you hear a lot of trucks on that road.

235
00:17:10,150 --> 00:17:14,070
ATTORNEY: Was it a single sound or more than one?

236
00:17:14,070 --> 00:17:17,984
WITNESS D: The first one was the big one. Then there were some other

237
00:17:17,984 --> 00:17:23,340
WITNESS D: sounds after, further away. Like scraping, and then another bang, further off.

238
00:17:23,340 --> 00:17:25,130
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Object to form.

239
00:17:25,130 --> 00:17:30,328
ATTORNEY: You can answer. Let me rephrase, actually. After the first loud sound,

240
00:17:30,328 --> 00:17:34,040
ATTORNEY: what else did you hear, in the order you heard it?

241
00:17:34,040 --> 00:17:39,165
WITNESS D: After the big bang, there was a kind of scraping, crashing noise that

242
00:17:39,165 --> 00:17:43,621
WITNESS D: kept going for a second or two. And then another thud a good

243
00:17:43,621 --> 00:17:48,300
WITNESS D: ways off, east. Then it got quiet, except for the truck engine.

244
00:17:48,300 --> 00:17:52,230
ATTORNEY: How did you know it was a truck engine?

245
00:17:52,230 --> 00:17:57,580
WITNESS D: You get to know the sound. Big diesel, idling. It was still running.

246
00:17:57,580 --> 00:18:01,500
ATTORNEY: Where were you when you heard the first bang?

247
00:18:01,500 --> 00:18:03,280
WITNESS D: Behind the register.

248
00:18:03,280 --> 00:18:05,420
ATTORNEY: What were you doing?

249
00:18:05,420 --> 00:18:09,700
WITNESS D: I was restocking the cigarette rack behind the counter.

250
00:18:09,700 --> 00:18:12,190
WITNESS D: I had my back half to the front.

251
00:18:12,190 --> 00:18:15,835
ATTORNEY: From where you were standing at that moment, could

252
00:18:15,835 --> 00:18:18,970
ATTORNEY: you see the eastbound lanes of the highway?

253
00:18:18,970 --> 00:18:24,320
WITNESS D: No. Not from back there. You can't see the road from the register.

254
00:18:24,320 --> 00:18:28,600
ATTORNEY: Could you see any part of the highway at all?

255
00:18:28,600 --> 00:18:34,168
WITNESS D: Maybe a little sliver at the top of the door glass, but you're looking

256
00:18:34,168 --> 00:18:38,940
WITNESS D: at the far side, and mostly you see the sky and the posters.

257
00:18:38,940 --> 00:18:41,790
ATTORNEY: Did you see the collision itself?

258
00:18:41,790 --> 00:18:46,070
WITNESS D: No. I did not see it. I only heard it.

259
00:18:46,070 --> 00:18:49,640
ATTORNEY: Did you see either vehicle before the sound?

260
00:18:49,640 --> 00:18:53,200
WITNESS D: No. I didn't see anything before the sound.

261
00:18:53,200 --> 00:18:56,770
ATTORNEY: What did you do after you heard it?

262
00:18:56,770 --> 00:18:59,813
WITNESS D: I put down what I was holding and I

263
00:18:59,813 --> 00:19:03,900
WITNESS D: went around the counter and out the front door.

264
00:19:03,900 --> 00:19:09,250
ATTORNEY: About how long did that take you, from the sound to getting outside?

265
00:19:09,250 --> 00:19:14,950
WITNESS D: Not long. Ten seconds maybe. Fifteen. I wasn't running exactly, but I was moving.

266
00:19:14,950 --> 00:19:16,740
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Object to form.

267
00:19:16,740 --> 00:19:19,230
ATTORNEY: Is that your best estimate?

268
00:19:19,230 --> 00:19:22,440
WITNESS D: That's my best estimate. It wasn't long.

269
00:19:22,440 --> 00:19:27,790
ATTORNEY: When you came out the front door, what's the first thing you noticed?

270
00:19:27,790 --> 00:19:32,495
WITNESS D: The truck. You couldn't miss it. A big white truck with the long

271
00:19:32,495 --> 00:19:37,420
WITNESS D: box trailer, stopped down 140th, past the store, on the south side.

272
00:19:37,420 --> 00:19:42,410
ATTORNEY: When you say down 140th, which direction is that from the store?

273
00:19:42,410 --> 00:19:47,427
WITNESS D: South. 140th runs off the highway going south, right along the side

274
00:19:47,427 --> 00:19:51,320
WITNESS D: of the store. The truck was down that road, past us.

275
00:19:51,320 --> 00:19:55,250
ATTORNEY: Was the truck moving when you first saw it?

276
00:19:55,250 --> 00:20:00,240
WITNESS D: No. It was stopped. The engine was still running, like I said.

277
00:20:00,240 --> 00:20:05,230
ATTORNEY: Was the trailer still out across the highway when you came out?

278
00:20:05,230 --> 00:20:10,797
WITNESS D: No. The whole thing was down on 140th by then. The back of it was past

279
00:20:10,797 --> 00:20:17,000
WITNESS D: the store, sort of even with the back of the building, maybe a little further.

280
00:20:17,000 --> 00:20:21,990
ATTORNEY: Could you see whether the truck was on the pavement of 140th?

281
00:20:21,990 --> 00:20:25,928
WITNESS D: It was on the road. I don't remember if it was

282
00:20:25,928 --> 00:20:30,550
WITNESS D: all the way on the pavement or partly on the shoulder.

283
00:20:30,550 --> 00:20:34,110
ATTORNEY: Did you notice anything about the trailer itself?

284
00:20:34,110 --> 00:20:39,584
WITNESS D: The side of it was damaged. There was a long scrape and the bottom

285
00:20:39,584 --> 00:20:44,810
WITNESS D: edge was torn up. I could see that from the front of the store.

286
00:20:44,810 --> 00:20:47,310
ATTORNEY: Which side of the trailer?

287
00:20:47,310 --> 00:20:49,450
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Object to form. Foundation.

288
00:20:49,450 --> 00:20:51,230
ATTORNEY: If you know.

289
00:20:51,230 --> 00:20:56,061
WITNESS D: The side facing the store, I believe. I was looking at it from

290
00:20:56,061 --> 00:21:00,815
WITNESS D: the front of the store, so it would be that side, facing west

291
00:21:00,815 --> 00:21:05,490
WITNESS D: and toward us. I'm not real sure which side you'd call that.

292
00:21:05,490 --> 00:21:09,410
ATTORNEY: That's fine. Did you go over to the truck?

293
00:21:09,410 --> 00:21:12,620
WITNESS D: No. I didn't go to the truck.

294
00:21:12,620 --> 00:21:16,900
ATTORNEY: After you noticed the truck, what else did you see?

295
00:21:16,900 --> 00:21:23,308
WITNESS D: I looked out at the highway and there wasn't a car anywhere near the intersection.

296
00:21:23,308 --> 00:21:28,310
WITNESS D: And then I looked east and I saw the car way down, off the road.

297
00:21:28,310 --> 00:21:31,160
ATTORNEY: Off the road on which side?

298
00:21:31,160 --> 00:21:36,510
WITNESS D: The south side. The same side as the store, just way down east.

299
00:21:36,510 --> 00:21:39,370
ATTORNEY: How far down would you estimate?

300
00:21:39,370 --> 00:21:44,288
WITNESS D: Far. I'm not good with distances. A few hundred yards, maybe? It was

301
00:21:44,288 --> 00:21:49,350
WITNESS D: down past where the fences are, in somebody's yard. Near a power pole.

302
00:21:49,350 --> 00:21:51,130
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Object to form.

303
00:21:51,130 --> 00:21:56,840
ATTORNEY: Do you know whether it was in a yard, or are you assuming that?

304
00:21:56,840 --> 00:22:01,795
WITNESS D: I know the area. There's houses down that way with fenced yards.

305
00:22:01,795 --> 00:22:05,822
WITNESS D: It looked like it was in one of those yards. I could

306
00:22:05,822 --> 00:22:10,390
WITNESS D: see it had gone through a fence because the fence was down.

307
00:22:10,390 --> 00:22:15,380
ATTORNEY: Could you see the car clearly from in front of the store?

308
00:22:15,380 --> 00:22:19,421
WITNESS D: Not clearly. I could see it was a dark car. I could

309
00:22:19,421 --> 00:22:24,650
WITNESS D: see it was sitting there, stopped. That's about all from that far.

310
00:22:24,650 --> 00:22:29,640
ATTORNEY: Was there any vehicle traffic on the eastbound lanes at that point?

311
00:22:29,640 --> 00:22:34,472
WITNESS D: Cars were stopping. A couple of cars pulled over on the shoulder.

312
00:22:34,472 --> 00:22:38,560
WITNESS D: One stopped right out in the lane with its flashers on.

313
00:22:38,560 --> 00:22:40,700
ATTORNEY: And the westbound side?

314
00:22:40,700 --> 00:22:44,633
WITNESS D: Some people slowed down, and I think one pickup pulled into

315
00:22:44,633 --> 00:22:48,900
WITNESS D: the median crossover and stopped there. People were getting out.

316
00:22:48,900 --> 00:22:53,890
ATTORNEY: Did you see anybody go toward the car down to the east?

317
00:22:53,890 --> 00:22:59,950
WITNESS D: Yes, a couple of men from the cars that stopped went running down that way.

318
00:22:59,950 --> 00:23:02,450
ATTORNEY: Did you go down there?

319
00:23:02,450 --> 00:23:05,300
WITNESS D: No. I never went down there.

320
00:23:05,300 --> 00:23:06,730
ATTORNEY: Why not?

321
00:23:06,730 --> 00:23:12,657
WITNESS D: I had the store. I couldn't just leave it open. And honestly, there were already

322
00:23:12,657 --> 00:23:18,140
WITNESS D: people going, and I didn't think I'd be any help. I thought I should call.

323
00:23:18,140 --> 00:23:20,280
ATTORNEY: Did you call anyone?

324
00:23:20,280 --> 00:23:24,789
WITNESS D: I went back in and called 911 from the store phone. But they

325
00:23:24,789 --> 00:23:29,900
WITNESS D: said they already had calls coming in, and they were sending people.

326
00:23:29,900 --> 00:23:33,470
ATTORNEY: About how long were you on that call?

327
00:23:33,470 --> 00:23:38,980
WITNESS D: A minute or two. They asked where, and I told them the store at 140th

328
00:23:38,980 --> 00:23:44,809
WITNESS D: and the highway. They asked if anybody was hurt, and I told them I didn't

329
00:23:44,809 --> 00:23:49,520
WITNESS D: know, the car was way down the road and I hadn't gone down.

330
00:23:49,520 --> 00:23:52,370
ATTORNEY: Did you then go back outside?

331
00:23:52,370 --> 00:23:54,150
WITNESS D: Yes. Right away.

332
00:23:54,150 --> 00:23:58,680
ATTORNEY: When you went outside, either the first time or the second

333
00:23:58,680 --> 00:24:02,350
ATTORNEY: time, did you see anyone in front of the store?

334
00:24:02,350 --> 00:24:06,630
WITNESS D: Yes. There was a woman out front of the store.

335
00:24:06,630 --> 00:24:11,620
ATTORNEY: Was that the same woman who'd been in earlier and bought groceries?

336
00:24:11,620 --> 00:24:16,260
WITNESS D: I think so. I believe so. She had the same bag.

337
00:24:16,260 --> 00:24:18,040
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Object to form.

338
00:24:18,040 --> 00:24:23,750
ATTORNEY: Did you notice her the first time you came out, or the second time?

339
00:24:23,750 --> 00:24:29,617
WITNESS D: The first time, I really only looked at the truck and down the road. I think

340
00:24:29,617 --> 00:24:35,870
WITNESS D: she was there, but I didn't really notice her until I came back out from calling.

341
00:24:35,870 --> 00:24:39,440
ATTORNEY: When you did notice her, where was she?

342
00:24:39,440 --> 00:24:43,000
WITNESS D: Out front. Outside, out front of the store.

343
00:24:43,000 --> 00:24:46,570
ATTORNEY: Can you be any more specific than that?

344
00:24:46,570 --> 00:24:50,512
WITNESS D: Not really. She was out front. I came out the door and

345
00:24:50,512 --> 00:24:55,840
WITNESS D: she was right there, outside. I wasn't paying attention to exactly where.

346
00:24:55,840 --> 00:24:58,340
ATTORNEY: Was she standing or sitting?

347
00:24:58,340 --> 00:25:00,830
WITNESS D: Standing, when I saw her.

348
00:25:00,830 --> 00:25:03,680
ATTORNEY: Can you describe how she appeared?

349
00:25:03,680 --> 00:25:07,210
WITNESS D: She was really upset. She was crying and she

350
00:25:07,210 --> 00:25:10,820
WITNESS D: had her hand over her mouth. She was shaking.

351
00:25:10,820 --> 00:25:12,600
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Object to form.

352
00:25:12,600 --> 00:25:17,950
ATTORNEY: I'm only asking what you observed. Did she appear injured in any way?

353
00:25:17,950 --> 00:25:22,230
WITNESS D: No. She wasn't hurt. She was just very shook up.

354
00:25:22,230 --> 00:25:25,080
ATTORNEY: Did you go over to her?

355
00:25:25,080 --> 00:25:29,710
WITNESS D: Yes. I went over and asked her if she was okay.

356
00:25:29,710 --> 00:25:34,279
ATTORNEY: I'm going to come back to your conversation with her in a moment.

357
00:25:34,279 --> 00:25:38,566
ATTORNEY: Before I do, I want to make sure I understand the scene. When

358
00:25:38,566 --> 00:25:44,330
ATTORNEY: you were standing out front, could you see the intersection itself, the crossover?

359
00:25:44,330 --> 00:25:49,330
WITNESS D: Yes. From outside you can see the whole intersection. It's right there.

360
00:25:49,330 --> 00:25:53,250
ATTORNEY: Was there anything in the roadway at the intersection?

361
00:25:53,250 --> 00:25:57,491
WITNESS D: There was some debris. Pieces of things, glass, some bits of

362
00:25:57,491 --> 00:26:01,450
WITNESS D: metal or plastic in the eastbound lanes. Not big pieces.

363
00:26:01,450 --> 00:26:05,370
ATTORNEY: Did anyone move the truck while you were outside?

364
00:26:05,370 --> 00:26:10,720
WITNESS D: No. It stayed where it was the whole time I was out there.

365
00:26:10,720 --> 00:26:15,360
ATTORNEY: And the car down to the east, did it change position?

366
00:26:15,360 --> 00:26:20,350
WITNESS D: No. It stayed down there. Nobody moved it while I was there.

367
00:26:20,350 --> 00:26:24,980
ATTORNEY: About how long after the bang did the first deputy arrive?

368
00:26:24,980 --> 00:26:30,690
WITNESS D: Maybe ten minutes. Maybe a little longer. It felt longer than it was, probably.

369
00:26:30,690 --> 00:26:33,540
ATTORNEY: Where did the first deputy go?

370
00:26:33,540 --> 00:26:39,011
WITNESS D: The first car went right on past the store, down east to where the car

371
00:26:39,011 --> 00:26:44,950
WITNESS D: was. Then the ambulance and a fire truck came, and they went down there too.

372
00:26:44,950 --> 00:26:48,160
ATTORNEY: Did any deputy come to the store?

373
00:26:48,160 --> 00:26:51,559
WITNESS D: Later on, yes. A while after. One came up

374
00:26:51,559 --> 00:26:55,290
WITNESS D: to the store and asked who had seen anything.

375
00:26:55,290 --> 00:26:58,997
ATTORNEY: We'll get to that. When you were standing out front

376
00:26:58,997 --> 00:27:03,140
ATTORNEY: with the woman, were there other people around the store?

377
00:27:03,140 --> 00:27:07,173
WITNESS D: A couple of people came over. One man who had stopped

378
00:27:07,173 --> 00:27:11,130
WITNESS D: his car came up and asked if we needed anything. And

379
00:27:11,130 --> 00:27:15,620
WITNESS D: the kids who'd been in earlier were across the parking lot.

380
00:27:15,620 --> 00:27:21,680
ATTORNEY: Was the bench shelter you described earlier there that afternoon, in front of the store?

381
00:27:21,680 --> 00:27:24,890
WITNESS D: Yes. It's always there. It was there.

382
00:27:24,890 --> 00:27:28,810
ATTORNEY: Did anything happen to the shelter in the crash?

383
00:27:28,810 --> 00:27:32,730
WITNESS D: No. Nothing touched it. Nothing touched the store either.

384
00:27:32,730 --> 00:27:38,800
ATTORNEY: When you were outside, how long did you stay out front before going back in?

385
00:27:38,800 --> 00:27:42,413
WITNESS D: I was in and out. I'd go in if somebody came

386
00:27:42,413 --> 00:27:47,257
WITNESS D: in to buy something, which a few did, people who'd stopped.

387
00:27:47,257 --> 00:27:51,280
WITNESS D: But mostly I was outside for the next hour or so.

388
00:27:51,280 --> 00:27:56,258
ATTORNEY: Let me go back to the moment you first walked out the door. I want to

389
00:27:56,258 --> 00:28:03,400
ATTORNEY: be precise. When you stepped out, was the truck already where you've described, stopped down 140th?

390
00:28:03,400 --> 00:28:08,390
WITNESS D: Yes. By the time I got out it was already stopped there.

391
00:28:08,390 --> 00:28:12,310
ATTORNEY: So you never saw the truck moving that afternoon?

392
00:28:12,310 --> 00:28:16,950
WITNESS D: Not before or after. I never saw it moving. Only stopped.

393
00:28:16,950 --> 00:28:20,870
ATTORNEY: And you never saw the car moving that afternoon?

394
00:28:20,870 --> 00:28:25,860
WITNESS D: No. When I saw it, it was already down there and stopped.

395
00:28:25,860 --> 00:28:30,002
ATTORNEY: I know I asked this, but I want the record clear.

396
00:28:30,002 --> 00:28:34,060
ATTORNEY: Did you see the car and the truck come together?

397
00:28:34,060 --> 00:28:35,850
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Asked and answered.

398
00:28:35,850 --> 00:28:37,630
ATTORNEY: You can answer.

399
00:28:37,630 --> 00:28:43,198
WITNESS D: No. I did not see it happen. I was inside behind the counter. I

400
00:28:43,198 --> 00:28:47,970
WITNESS D: heard it, and then I went out and saw what I told you.

401
00:28:47,970 --> 00:28:52,168
ATTORNEY: Thank you. Now, when you went over to the woman out

402
00:28:52,168 --> 00:28:56,530
ATTORNEY: front and asked her if she was okay, did she respond?

403
00:28:56,530 --> 00:29:01,261
WITNESS D: At first she couldn't really say anything. She was just shaking

404
00:29:01,261 --> 00:29:05,090
WITNESS D: her head and crying. I put my hand on her shoulder.

405
00:29:05,090 --> 00:29:07,940
ATTORNEY: Did she eventually talk with you?

406
00:29:07,940 --> 00:29:11,860
WITNESS D: Yes. After a minute or so, she started talking.

407
00:29:11,860 --> 00:29:14,710
ATTORNEY: Did she tell you her name?

408
00:29:14,710 --> 00:29:18,535
WITNESS D: Her first name. And she said she was waiting

409
00:29:18,535 --> 00:29:21,490
WITNESS D: on her sister to come pick her up.

410
00:29:21,490 --> 00:29:25,410
ATTORNEY: Did she tell you when her sister was coming?

411
00:29:25,410 --> 00:29:26,840
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Objection, hearsay.

412
00:29:26,840 --> 00:29:28,620
ATTORNEY: You can answer.

413
00:29:28,620 --> 00:29:33,255
WITNESS D: She said her sister was supposed to be there around five. And

414
00:29:33,255 --> 00:29:37,890
WITNESS D: her sister did come, a little before or around five, I think.

415
00:29:37,890 --> 00:29:41,772
ATTORNEY: Before the sister arrived, did the woman stay out

416
00:29:41,772 --> 00:29:45,020
ATTORNEY: front the whole time, as far as you know?

417
00:29:45,020 --> 00:29:50,730
WITNESS D: As far as I know. She was out there whenever I was out there.

418
00:29:50,730 --> 00:29:56,080
ATTORNEY: Did you ever see her go down toward the car to the east?

419
00:29:56,080 --> 00:30:00,000
WITNESS D: No. She didn't go down there. She stayed by the store.

420
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:07,173
ATTORNEY: Let's pick up where we left off. You told us that when you came out the

421
00:30:07,173 --> 00:30:14,750
ATTORNEY: front door, you saw a woman outside, out front of the store. Is that right?

422
00:30:14,750 --> 00:30:16,980
WITNESS D: Yes. That's right.

423
00:30:16,980 --> 00:30:21,450
ATTORNEY: Had you ever seen her before that afternoon?

424
00:30:21,450 --> 00:30:29,053
WITNESS D: I think she'd been in earlier. She bought a few things, maybe twenty minutes before.

425
00:30:29,053 --> 00:30:35,750
WITNESS D: I remember her because she asked if she could wait out front for her ride.

426
00:30:35,750 --> 00:30:39,330
ATTORNEY: And what did you tell her?

427
00:30:39,330 --> 00:30:46,930
WITNESS D: I told her sure, people do it all the time. There's the bench out there.

428
00:30:46,930 --> 00:30:54,080
ATTORNEY: When you came outside after the bang, did you go to her right away?

429
00:30:54,080 --> 00:30:59,964
WITNESS D: Pretty much. She was the first person I saw. She was upset,

430
00:30:59,964 --> 00:31:05,250
WITNESS D: and she was saying something, and I went over to her.

431
00:31:05,250 --> 00:31:08,830
ATTORNEY: Did the two of you talk?

432
00:31:08,830 --> 00:31:10,170
WITNESS D: Yes.

433
00:31:10,170 --> 00:31:15,980
ATTORNEY: What, if anything, did she tell you about what she saw?

434
00:31:15,980 --> 00:31:17,770
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Objection, hearsay.

435
00:31:17,770 --> 00:31:20,000
ATTORNEY: You can answer.

436
00:31:20,000 --> 00:31:25,572
WITNESS D: She said she had a clear view of the car the whole

437
00:31:25,572 --> 00:31:31,590
WITNESS D: way in. She said she watched it right up until it hit.

438
00:31:31,590 --> 00:31:36,940
ATTORNEY: Do you remember anything else she said in that conversation?

439
00:31:36,940 --> 00:31:38,720
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Same objection.

440
00:31:38,720 --> 00:31:45,569
WITNESS D: She kept saying, oh my God, oh my God. She said it didn't stop. Something

441
00:31:45,569 --> 00:31:52,980
WITNESS D: like that. And she kept looking down the road, east, toward where the car went.

442
00:31:52,980 --> 00:31:57,940
ATTORNEY: When she told you she had a clear view of the

443
00:31:57,940 --> 00:32:03,230
ATTORNEY: car, how soon was that after you heard the bang?

444
00:32:03,230 --> 00:32:09,470
WITNESS D: Right away. A minute, maybe less. I'd just come out the door.

445
00:32:09,470 --> 00:32:13,040
ATTORNEY: Did you ask her any questions?

446
00:32:13,040 --> 00:32:17,343
WITNESS D: I asked her if she was okay. I asked her

447
00:32:17,343 --> 00:32:22,400
WITNESS D: what happened. I think that's when she told me.

448
00:32:22,400 --> 00:32:28,190
ATTORNEY: So she told you in response to you asking what happened?

449
00:32:28,190 --> 00:32:33,540
WITNESS D: Yes. I said, what happened, and that's what she said.

450
00:32:33,540 --> 00:32:39,780
ATTORNEY: How would you describe the way she was acting at that point?

451
00:32:39,780 --> 00:32:42,010
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Objection to form.

452
00:32:42,010 --> 00:32:44,230
ATTORNEY: You can answer.

453
00:32:44,230 --> 00:32:50,712
WITNESS D: She was shaking. Her hands were shaking. She had a shopping bag and

454
00:32:50,712 --> 00:32:56,710
WITNESS D: she kind of dropped it down by her feet. She was talking fast.

455
00:32:56,710 --> 00:32:58,940
ATTORNEY: Was she crying?

456
00:32:58,940 --> 00:33:04,740
WITNESS D: A little. More just shaken up. Like she couldn't believe it.

457
00:33:04,740 --> 00:33:08,300
ATTORNEY: Did you do anything for her?

458
00:33:08,300 --> 00:33:14,874
WITNESS D: I went back inside and got her a bottle of water out of the

459
00:33:14,874 --> 00:33:21,670
WITNESS D: cooler. And I brought it out to her and told her to sit down.

460
00:33:21,670 --> 00:33:24,350
ATTORNEY: Did she sit down?

461
00:33:24,350 --> 00:33:28,331
WITNESS D: For a little bit, on the bench. Then she

462
00:33:28,331 --> 00:33:32,810
WITNESS D: stood back up. She couldn't really sit still.

463
00:33:32,810 --> 00:33:36,820
ATTORNEY: How long were you outside with her?

464
00:33:36,820 --> 00:33:43,141
WITNESS D: Off and on, maybe a half hour. I had to go back in a couple

465
00:33:43,141 --> 00:33:50,640
WITNESS D: of times. I had the register and I couldn't just leave the store open.

466
00:33:50,640 --> 00:33:56,430
ATTORNEY: Was anyone else working in the store with you that afternoon?

467
00:33:56,430 --> 00:34:02,230
WITNESS D: No. Just me. Saturdays it's usually just one person until five.

468
00:34:02,230 --> 00:34:06,690
ATTORNEY: Did you lock the store at any point?

469
00:34:06,690 --> 00:34:12,826
WITNESS D: No. I thought about it. But people started coming in asking to

470
00:34:12,826 --> 00:34:18,270
WITNESS D: use the phone and the bathroom, so I just left it open.

471
00:34:18,270 --> 00:34:24,510
ATTORNEY: While you were outside with her, did she make any phone calls?

472
00:34:24,510 --> 00:34:31,837
WITNESS D: She called somebody. Her sister, I think. She said her sister was coming to get

473
00:34:31,837 --> 00:34:38,330
WITNESS D: her and she needed to tell her what happened, to be careful coming in.

474
00:34:38,330 --> 00:34:41,450
ATTORNEY: Did her sister eventually arrive?

475
00:34:41,450 --> 00:34:47,352
WITNESS D: Yes. Around five, I think. Maybe a little before. A woman

476
00:34:47,352 --> 00:34:51,700
WITNESS D: pulled in and she got in the car with her.

477
00:34:51,700 --> 00:34:54,820
ATTORNEY: Before that, did deputies arrive?

478
00:34:54,820 --> 00:35:00,610
WITNESS D: Yes. They got there pretty fast. Ten minutes, maybe fifteen.

479
00:35:00,610 --> 00:35:04,180
WITNESS D: First one car and then a lot of them.

480
00:35:04,180 --> 00:35:09,080
ATTORNEY: Where did the deputies go first, if you know?

481
00:35:09,080 --> 00:35:14,753
WITNESS D: I saw them go down the road, east, toward where the car

482
00:35:14,753 --> 00:35:20,220
WITNESS D: ended up. And some went over to the truck down 140th.

483
00:35:20,220 --> 00:35:24,680
ATTORNEY: Did any deputy speak with you that afternoon?

484
00:35:24,680 --> 00:35:31,085
WITNESS D: Yes. One came up to the store a while later. He asked if I

485
00:35:31,085 --> 00:35:37,600
WITNESS D: saw anything. I told him no, I was inside, I just heard it.

486
00:35:37,600 --> 00:35:42,060
ATTORNEY: Did he take your name and phone number?

487
00:35:42,060 --> 00:35:47,860
WITNESS D: Yes. He wrote it down. And he asked about the cameras.

488
00:35:47,860 --> 00:35:51,870
ATTORNEY: What did he ask about the cameras?

489
00:35:51,870 --> 00:35:53,650
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Objection, hearsay.

490
00:35:53,650 --> 00:35:58,550
ATTORNEY: I'm not offering it for the truth. Go ahead.

491
00:35:58,550 --> 00:36:04,181
WITNESS D: He asked if we had any cameras that pointed at the road.

492
00:36:04,181 --> 00:36:09,409
WITNESS D: And I told him we have one over the register and one

493
00:36:09,409 --> 00:36:15,040
WITNESS D: at the back door. Nothing that looks out at the highway.

494
00:36:15,040 --> 00:36:19,500
ATTORNEY: Is that accurate, as far as you know?

495
00:36:19,500 --> 00:36:25,478
WITNESS D: Yes. The one inside just shows the counter. You can't see anything

496
00:36:25,478 --> 00:36:30,640
WITNESS D: out the windows on it. The windows are covered up anyway.

497
00:36:30,640 --> 00:36:36,880
ATTORNEY: Did you see the deputy speak with the woman from out front?

498
00:36:36,880 --> 00:36:43,120
WITNESS D: Yes. He talked with her for a while. Longer than with me.

499
00:36:43,120 --> 00:36:47,130
ATTORNEY: Could you hear what she told him?

500
00:36:47,130 --> 00:36:54,710
WITNESS D: No. I was back inside by then. I just saw them standing out there talking.

501
00:36:54,710 --> 00:36:58,720
ATTORNEY: Did you later give a written statement?

502
00:36:58,720 --> 00:37:03,690
WITNESS D: Yes. A few days later. A deputy came back to the

503
00:37:03,690 --> 00:37:08,970
WITNESS D: store and asked me to write down what I remembered.

504
00:37:08,970 --> 00:37:12,980
ATTORNEY: Do you remember what day that was?

505
00:37:12,980 --> 00:37:18,770
WITNESS D: It was the next week. Tuesday or Wednesday. I was working.

506
00:37:18,770 --> 00:37:26,350
ATTORNEY: I'm going to hand you what's been marked as Exhibit 2. Do you recognize this?

507
00:37:26,350 --> 00:37:30,360
WITNESS D: Yes. That's my statement. That's my handwriting.

508
00:37:30,360 --> 00:37:37,490
ATTORNEY: Take a moment and read it to yourself, and tell me when you're done.

509
00:37:37,490 --> 00:37:39,720
WITNESS D: Okay. I'm done.

510
00:37:39,720 --> 00:37:45,960
ATTORNEY: Is that a true and accurate copy of the statement you wrote?

511
00:37:45,960 --> 00:37:49,080
WITNESS D: Yes. It looks like it.

512
00:37:49,080 --> 00:37:53,980
ATTORNEY: Is there anything in it that you'd change today?

513
00:37:53,980 --> 00:38:00,133
WITNESS D: No. It's short. It just says I was inside, I heard a loud

514
00:38:00,133 --> 00:38:06,394
WITNESS D: bang, I went outside, I saw the truck and the car down the

515
00:38:06,394 --> 00:38:11,360
WITNESS D: road, and a lady out front told me she saw it.

516
00:38:11,360 --> 00:38:16,270
ATTORNEY: Does your statement say what the lady told you?

517
00:38:16,270 --> 00:38:24,290
WITNESS D: It says she told me she saw the whole thing. I didn't write down every word.

518
00:38:24,290 --> 00:38:32,310
ATTORNEY: When you wrote that, were you trying to put down what she said, or a summary?

519
00:38:32,310 --> 00:38:34,540
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Objection to form.

520
00:38:34,540 --> 00:38:42,120
WITNESS D: A summary, I guess. That's what I remembered. That she saw it the whole time.

521
00:38:42,120 --> 00:38:47,020
ATTORNEY: Did you talk with her again after that day?

522
00:38:47,020 --> 00:38:53,700
WITNESS D: No. I never saw her again. I don't think she's been back in.

523
00:38:53,700 --> 00:39:00,390
ATTORNEY: Did you talk about what happened with anyone else, other than the deputies?

524
00:39:00,390 --> 00:39:05,610
WITNESS D: My manager. I called him that evening and told him. And

525
00:39:05,610 --> 00:39:10,640
WITNESS D: people in town asked about it for a while. Customers.

526
00:39:10,640 --> 00:39:17,330
ATTORNEY: Did you tell your manager what the woman out front said to you?

527
00:39:17,330 --> 00:39:24,460
WITNESS D: I told him there was a lady outside who saw it. That's about all.

528
00:39:24,460 --> 00:39:29,546
ATTORNEY: Let me go back to that afternoon for a moment. At

529
00:39:29,546 --> 00:39:35,150
ATTORNEY: any point did you walk down to either of the vehicles?

530
00:39:35,150 --> 00:39:37,830
WITNESS D: No. I never did.

531
00:39:37,830 --> 00:39:39,610
ATTORNEY: Why not?

532
00:39:39,610 --> 00:39:46,026
WITNESS D: I didn't want to. And there were already people going down there. People

533
00:39:46,026 --> 00:39:51,640
WITNESS D: who'd stopped. And then the deputies. I stayed up by the store.

534
00:39:51,640 --> 00:39:56,100
ATTORNEY: Did you walk down 140th toward the truck?

535
00:39:56,100 --> 00:40:04,120
WITNESS D: No. I could see it from the front of the store. I didn't go down there.

536
00:40:04,120 --> 00:40:11,250
ATTORNEY: From where you were, out front of the store, could you see the car?

537
00:40:11,250 --> 00:40:16,705
WITNESS D: Off in the distance. Down to the east, off the road,

538
00:40:16,705 --> 00:40:21,950
WITNESS D: by the pole. I could see it was there. That's all.

539
00:40:21,950 --> 00:40:27,300
ATTORNEY: Did anyone from the store go down to the vehicles?

540
00:40:27,300 --> 00:40:30,860
WITNESS D: No. It was just me working.

541
00:40:30,860 --> 00:40:38,440
ATTORNEY: Did you notice anything about the road itself after the crash? Anything on the pavement?

542
00:40:38,440 --> 00:40:44,010
WITNESS D: There was some stuff in the road. Pieces. I couldn't tell you

543
00:40:44,010 --> 00:40:49,580
WITNESS D: what. The deputies closed the eastbound side for a long time.

544
00:40:49,580 --> 00:40:52,700
ATTORNEY: How long, if you know?

545
00:40:52,700 --> 00:40:58,940
WITNESS D: Hours. It was still closed when I left. I left around eight.

546
00:40:58,940 --> 00:41:04,740
ATTORNEY: Were you still at the store when the truck was moved?

547
00:41:04,740 --> 00:41:11,870
WITNESS D: No. It was still down there when I left. They had lights set up.

548
00:41:11,870 --> 00:41:15,715
ATTORNEY: All right. I think that's all I have for

549
00:41:15,715 --> 00:41:20,330
ATTORNEY: now. Thank you. Counsel may have some questions.

550
00:41:20,330 --> 00:41:24,350
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Thank you. Just a few. Good afternoon.

551
00:41:24,350 --> 00:41:26,130
WITNESS D: Good afternoon.

552
00:41:26,130 --> 00:41:30,838
OPPOSING COUNSEL: I want to make sure the record is clear. You did

553
00:41:30,838 --> 00:41:36,820
OPPOSING COUNSEL: not see the collision between the car and the truck, correct?

554
00:41:36,820 --> 00:41:39,940
WITNESS D: Correct. I didn't see it.

555
00:41:39,940 --> 00:41:45,740
OPPOSING COUNSEL: You were inside the store, at the register, when it happened?

556
00:41:45,740 --> 00:41:47,080
WITNESS D: Yes.

557
00:41:47,080 --> 00:41:53,760
OPPOSING COUNSEL: And from the register you can't see the eastbound lanes of the highway?

558
00:41:53,760 --> 00:42:01,340
WITNESS D: No. Not with the posters and the cooler. You can't see the road from there.

559
00:42:01,340 --> 00:42:06,240
OPPOSING COUNSEL: So you didn't see the car approaching the intersection?

560
00:42:06,240 --> 00:42:07,580
WITNESS D: No.

561
00:42:07,580 --> 00:42:12,480
OPPOSING COUNSEL: And you didn't see the truck making its turn?

562
00:42:12,480 --> 00:42:18,270
WITNESS D: No. When I came out, it was already down 140th, stopped.

563
00:42:18,270 --> 00:42:23,644
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Before you heard the bang, had you seen the woman from

564
00:42:23,644 --> 00:42:28,520
OPPOSING COUNSEL: out front at any time after she left the counter?

565
00:42:28,520 --> 00:42:35,210
WITNESS D: No. I was doing other things. Stocking a little. I didn't look out.

566
00:42:35,210 --> 00:42:43,230
OPPOSING COUNSEL: So you don't know where she was standing at the moment the car reached the intersection?

567
00:42:43,230 --> 00:42:46,800
ATTORNEY: Objection, asked and answered. Go ahead.

568
00:42:46,800 --> 00:42:54,370
WITNESS D: No. I didn't see her until after. When I came out, she was out front.

569
00:42:54,370 --> 00:42:59,575
OPPOSING COUNSEL: You don't know whether she moved between the time of

570
00:42:59,575 --> 00:43:04,180
OPPOSING COUNSEL: the impact and the time you came out the door?

571
00:43:04,180 --> 00:43:06,410
ATTORNEY: Objection to form.

572
00:43:06,410 --> 00:43:10,420
WITNESS D: I don't know. I wasn't out there.

573
00:43:10,420 --> 00:43:15,241
OPPOSING COUNSEL: How long would you say it took you to get from

574
00:43:15,241 --> 00:43:21,110
OPPOSING COUNSEL: the register to the front door after you heard the bang?

575
00:43:21,110 --> 00:43:29,140
WITNESS D: A few seconds. Maybe ten. I kind of froze for a second, and then I went.

576
00:43:29,140 --> 00:43:34,085
OPPOSING COUNSEL: And everything you've told us about what she saw, that's

577
00:43:34,085 --> 00:43:38,500
OPPOSING COUNSEL: what she told you, not something you saw yourself?

578
00:43:38,500 --> 00:43:42,950
WITNESS D: Right. That's just what she said to me.

579
00:43:42,950 --> 00:43:48,300
OPPOSING COUNSEL: You'd agree she was very upset when she said it?

580
00:43:48,300 --> 00:43:50,530
ATTORNEY: Objection to form.

581
00:43:50,530 --> 00:43:53,200
WITNESS D: Yes. She was upset.

582
00:43:53,200 --> 00:43:57,660
OPPOSING COUNSEL: You didn't ask her where she'd been standing?

583
00:43:57,660 --> 00:44:01,670
WITNESS D: No. I didn't think to ask that.

584
00:44:01,670 --> 00:44:04,790
OPPOSING COUNSEL: And she didn't tell you?

585
00:44:04,790 --> 00:44:07,910
WITNESS D: No. Not that I remember.

586
00:44:07,910 --> 00:44:11,480
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Thank you. That's all I have.

587
00:44:11,480 --> 00:44:17,586
ATTORNEY: Just one follow-up. When she told you she had a clear view

588
00:44:17,586 --> 00:44:23,060
ATTORNEY: of the car, did she seem unsure about it in any way?

589
00:44:23,060 --> 00:44:26,180
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Objection, foundation, calls for speculation.

590
00:44:26,180 --> 00:44:31,980
WITNESS D: She didn't sound unsure. She said it like she was sure.

591
00:44:31,980 --> 00:44:34,650
ATTORNEY: Thank you. Nothing further.

592
00:44:34,650 --> 00:44:40,000
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Nothing further from me. The witness will read and sign.

593
00:44:40,000 --> 00:44:51,837
VIDEOGRAPHER: This concludes the videotaped deposition of Witness D. The

594
00:44:51,837 --> 00:45:00,000
VIDEOGRAPHER: time is 2:15 p.m. We are off the record.
